hadiths[2]{hadithnumber,text}:
"1080","On the authority of Bundar, on the authority of Muhammad, meaning Ibn Ja’far, on the authority of Shu’bah, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Asim, who is Ibn Damrah, on the authority of Ali, who said: “Who The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, recited the Witr prayer throughout the night, from its beginning, middle, and end.”"
"1081","Bahr bin Nasr narrated to us, Abdullah bin Wahb narrated to us, he said: Muawiyah bin Salih narrated to me, that Abdullah bin Abi Qais narrated to him, that Aisha, the wife of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, asked: How did the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, perform the Witr prayer, at the end of the night or the beginning of it? She said: He used to do all of that, perhaps “the Witr prayer at the beginning of the night and sometimes at the end of it, so I said: Praise be to God who has made the matter expansive.”"
